# PWA Requirements (mandatory)

Trenio.by is a **100% PWA-compatible** project. Treat every change as part of an installable web app.

## Before shipping UI or routing changes

- [ ] Works in standalone display mode (no broken layout without browser chrome)
- [ ] No hard dependency on APIs unavailable offline without graceful fallback
- [ ] Static assets/icons go in `public/` when added
- [ ] New routes consider offline UX (message, not blank screen)
- [ ] SSR hydration succeeds (no client-only crashes on first paint)
- [ ] Auth cookies remain HttpOnly; scope compatible with PWA origin

## Target artifacts (implement when touching PWA)

- `public/manifest.webmanifest`
- Service worker + cache strategy
- `/offline` route
- Icons 192×192, 512×512

## When adding features

Ask: *Does this break installability, caching, or offline behavior?*

If yes — add fallback or document in `docs/TECH_SPEC.md` §6.

Use skill `.cursor/skills/trenio-pwa-audit/` for full audit checklist.
